  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Ethan Park and Owen Carter putt best on the team, and the two measures split the top spot between them.\n\n- **Strokes gained putting:** Ethan Park is first at -1.92 strokes per round over his last 8 recorded rounds. Owen Carter is second at -2.06 over his last 8.\n- **Putts per round:** Owen Carter is lowest at 31.88 over his last 8 rounds. Tyler Hayes is next at 32.29 over his last 7. Ethan Park is third at 32.5 over his last 8.\n\nThe gap between Ethan and Owen on strokes gained is small, so I wouldn't separate them on putting alone. Strokes gained also adjusts for how far the putts were, which putts per round doesn't.\n\nEvery player with data is below zero on strokes gained putting. The team average is -3.01, and the PGA Tour baseline is 0. There is no college figure for strokes gained, so I can't place anyone against the Division I average. Ethan and Owen are the least negative on the team, not positive putters.\n\nEach player's last ten rounds actually number 7 or 8 putting rounds. They run from late May or June through September 26. Cole Bennett's window runs later, to October 21. Audit Testplayer has no recorded rounds, so this covers 7 of your 8 players.",
